notes: |
  CSS consolidation Phase 1 — declarative cascade.

  Problem: 14 classes overlap between components.css (newer) and
  legacy.css (older). Today cascade resolved by import order
  (legacy.css imported last → legacy wins) — WRONG direction for
  .piano-key and .step-grid* since components actually use newer
  styles.

  Solution: CSS cascade layers in index.css. Single @layer
  declaration sets priority:
    tokens < base < legacy < components < sheets < icons < landing

  Result:
    - 11 conflicts: no-op (legacy applies, components only
      references classes in touch-target lists / selectors)
    - 3 conflicts (.piano-key, .step-grid + 8 child classes) now
      correctly apply components.css (the design PianoKeyboard.tsx
      and StepGrid.tsx actually use)
    - Future refactor can drop legacy.css without cascade surprises

  Bonus fix: BottomToolstrip was unclickable on mobile because
  position-less vs TabBar's position:fixed + higher z-index. Added
  position:fixed + bottom offset + z-index above tabbar.

  Verification:
    - typecheck: clean (pnpm typecheck)
    - vitest: 628/628 passing
    - lint: 2 errors (preexisting, unchanged)
    - build (vite): succeeds, output CSS contains @layer declaration
      + piano-key + step-grid rules in both layers with components
      winning by layer priority order
    - dev server smoke test (playwright): TopBar/PresetRow/
      TransportPanel/BottomToolstrip/TabBar render correctly. Found
      BottomToolstrip z-index bug → fixed in 5e03b8d.

  Audit summary:
    - legacy.css unique classes: 120
    - components.css unique classes: 140
    - overlap: 14
    - behavioral change: 3 (.piano-key, .step-grid*)

  Not done (deferred):
    - Drop legacy.css entirely (separate packet; layer-based eating
      is safer than monolithic merge)
    - Migrate unique-to-legacy classes to components.css
    - Replace inline critical CSS in dist/index.html with @layer-aware
      inline subset